---A `HitmarkType` config contains data about the various hitmark overlays that can be drawn above an entity.
---
---These config types can be found within the `config.Hitmark` table:
---
---Info: A `HitmarkType` is a Proxy usertype, which means it is safe to copy and store in your scripts. It cannot,
---however, be used with any persistent storage.
---
---Information available within an `HitmarkType` includes:
---@class HitmarkType
---@field id integer (Read-only) The ID of this config type.
---@field configName string (Read-only) The name of this config, i.e. `"MAGIC_DAMAGE"`.
---@field typeName string (Read-only) The type of this config. Will always be `"Hitmark"`.
---@field duration integer (Read-only) How long, in client ticks, the hitmark will display for.
